{{Quote|Do you think I came to the most unfindable place in the galaxy for no reason at all?|Luke Skywalker|<ref name="The Last Jedi">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>}}
'''Temple Island'''<ref name="HC 72">{{HelmetCollectionCite|72|Highlights of the Saga}}</ref> was an island on the [[planet]] [[Ahch-To]] where the [[Jedi Order]] was founded over a thousand generations before the [[Republic Era|fall]] of the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="TLJ VD" /> The island was where [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]] chose to spend the rest of his life in self-imposed [[Exile (punishment)|exile]] after his [[Skywalker family|nephew]], [[Ben Solo]], [[Destruction of the Jedi Temple|destroyed]] the new generation of Jedi. He was discovered on Temple Island by [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], a [[The Force|Force]] [[Force-sensitive|prodigy]],<ref name="The Last Jedi" /> in [[34 ABY]].<ref name="Date note">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places the events of {{Film|VII}} in [[34 ABY]]. The events of {{Film|VIII}} pick up immediately following ''The Force Awakens''.</ref> Skywalker [[Death|died]] on the island after [[Force projection|projecting]] his appearance into the [[Battle of Crait]].<ref name="The Last Jedi" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Description==
{{Quote|You imagine an ocean. I see it. I see the island.|Kylo Ren|<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref>}}
The Temple Island<ref name="HC 72" /> was an island located in the northern latitudes of the [[planet]] [[Ahch-To]],<ref name="TLJ VD" /> between the [[Sea of Pallaskea]] and the [[Bonthian Sea]].<ref name="Galactic Atlas UE">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]''</ref> The island was home to the [[first Jedi Temple]] and a [[Jedi village]] where the first Jedi lived, which was maintained by [[Lanai]] [[Caretakers]]. The island was also home to the native [[porg]]s,<ref name="TLJ VD" /> [[insect]]s, and its steep slopes were a vivid, verdant [[Color|green]], with the tufts of emerald [[grass]] and the grayish [[moss]] that clung to slabs of rock.<ref name="TLJ EE" />

[[File:TLJ_Rey_inside_Uneti_Tree.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Rey visited the sacred uneti tree as the books called to her during her time on Ahch-To.]]
The island housed a trunk of the centuries-old<ref name="TLJ VD" /> [[Force-sensitive]] [[uneti tree]]<ref name="TSWB">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref> known as the [[Jedi Tree]].<ref name="Secrets of the Jedi">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Jedi]]''</ref> It was accessible by a stairway that led from the first Jedi Temple to the tree.<ref name="TLJ VD" /> Once upon a time the tree was massive, but over time it withered away, and all that remained of it by [[34 ABY]] was an ancient, mossy husk, with an opening, carved by weather and time.<ref name="TLJ EE" /> Three pulpy offshoots stood guard around a gigantic central trunk. All had tops splintered like jagged crowns, and none bore foliage or branches. Only [[moss]] grew on the ashen bark.<ref name="TLJ JN">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: A Junior Novel]]''</ref>

==History==
A thousand generations before 34 ABY,<ref name="Library Date">{{Film|VIII}} states that the library was built on [[Ahch-To]] a thousand generations before the events of the movie. ''Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary'' places ''The Last Jedi'' in the same year as {{Film|VII}}, which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[34 ABY]]. Therefore, the first Jedi Temple was built a thousand generations before 34 ABY.</ref> a [[tree library]] was built<ref name="The Last Jedi" /> within the hollowed-out trunk of the tree. A bookshelf within contained the original [[Sacred Jedi texts|sacred texts]] of the [[Jedi]] religion during the period of [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]]'s [[Exile (punishment)|exile]] on the island.<ref name="TLJ VD" /> As she climbed the steps of the island, [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] thought of it as a tiny dot on the [[water]], but that was a misperception&mdash;the island was the pinnacle of a [[mountain]] that began in darkness, rising from the bones of the planet far below.<ref name="TLJ EE" /> During Skywalker's exile, the [[Force spirit]] of [[Yoda]] initiated a lightning strike that set the uneti [[tree]] ablaze.<ref name="The Last Jedi" />

==Behind the scenes==
Temple Island is based on [[Skellig Michael]] in [[Wikipedia:Ireland|Ireland]], where the final scenes of {{Film|VII}} and parts of {{Film|VIII}} were filmed. Filming on the island itself was not an option for most of ''The Last Jedi''{{'s}} production, so some scenes were shot on location just north on the [[Wikipedia:Dingle Peninsula|Dingle Peninsula]], while others were shot at [[Wikipedia:Pinewood Studios|Pinewood Studios]] in [[Wikipedia:England|England]].<ref name="Art TLJ">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Last Jedi]]''</ref> The short stories "[[The Heart of a Jedi]]," "[[A Spark of Hope]]," and "[[The Final Battle]]" published in [[5-Minute Star Wars Stories (second edition)|''5-Minute Star Wars Stories'']] mistakenly identify Temple Island as Ahch-To, rather than the planet.<ref name="5 Min">[[5-Minute Star Wars Stories (second edition)|''5-Minute Star Wars Stories'', second edition]]</ref>

